780","person_slug":"peter-whish-wilson","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Rachel Siewert","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10584","person_slug":"rachel-siewert","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Richard Di Natale","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10755","person_slug":"richard-di-natale","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sarah Hanson-Young","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10711","person_slug":"sarah-hanson-young","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Scott Ryan","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10715","person_slug":"scott-ryan","vote":"no"},{"name":"Simon Birmingham","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10044","person_slug":"simon-birmingham","vote":"no"},{"name":"Skye Kakoschke-Moore","party":"Centre Alliance","person_id":"tvfy_10854","person_slug":"skye-kakoschke-moore","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Stirling Griff","party":"Centre Alliance","person_id":"tvfy_10851","person_slug":"stirling-griff","vote":"aye"}],"name":"Motions - Ministerial Standards - Former MP Ian Macfarlane","noes":27,"question":"The majority voted in favour of a [motion](http://www.openaustralia.org.au/senate/?id=2016-10-11.121.1) introduced by NSW Senator [Lee Rhiannon](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/senate/nsw/lee_rhiannon), which means it was successful. Motions like these don't have legal force, but do express the opinion of the Senate. ### Motion text > *That the Senate—* > *(1) notes that:* >> *(a) the statement of ministerial standards stipulates that \"Ministers are required to undertake that, for an eighteen month period after ceasing to be a Minister, they will not lobby, advocate or have business meetings with members of the government, parliament, public service or defence force on any matters on which they have had official dealings as Minister in their last eighteen months in office\";* >> *(b) Mr [Ian Macfarlane](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/representatives/groom/ian_macfarlane) held the Resources portfolio for the Coalition for thirteen years, including nine years as Minister, most recently the period of 18 September 2013 until 21 September 2015;* >> *(c) on 26 September 2016, approximately twelve months after he ceased to be a Minister, it was reported that Mr Macfarlane had been appointed as CEO of the Queensland Resources Council; and* >> *(d) it was also reported that Prime Minister [Turnbull](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/representatives/wentworth/malcolm_turnbull)'s office gave approval for Mr Macfarlane's appointment;* > *(2) calls on all federal Ministers to rule out meeting with Mr Macfarlane in his capacity as CEO of the Queensland Resources Council until 21 March 2017 when eighteen months will have elapsed after he ceased to hold his ministerial portfolios; and* > *(3) calls on Prime Minister Turnbull to clarify whether he or his office endorsed Mr Macfarlane's disregard for the statement of ministerial standards.*","result":"affirmative","slug":"division-federal-senate-4335","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2016-10-11/3"}
